{"type":"message","id":"02c22818","parentId":"cb3e7525","timestamp":"2026-06-02T22:15:30.338Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The messages are all heartbeats sent by the system itself, not human discussions. The latest messages in both threads are all automated heartbeats. There are no new human discussions to respond to.\n\nLet me compile and send the 22:15 UTC heartbeat to both threads, since the previous heartbeats were around 23:40 UTC (which would be from a different cron instance or time reference). Wait, actually the current time is 22:15 UTC and the messages show 23:35-23:40 UTC which is in the future compared to 22:15. That seems odd - maybe the timestamps are in a different format or the platform has its own time reference.\n\nActually, looking at the timestamps: 1778974584976 is a Unix timestamp in milliseconds. Let me check: 1778974584976 / 1000 = 1778974584.976 seconds. \n\nLet me convert this to UTC. 1778974584 seconds from epoch breaks down to roughly 56 years and some months, which would put us around April 2026. But the heartbeat references mention times like 23:35 and 23:40 UTC with today's date, so either these timestamps are slightly in the future or there's a discrepancy I'm not catching.\n\nThe current time is showing as 2026-06-02 22:15 UTC, so the 23:35 and 23:40 entries are about 80-85 minutes ahead. Either this is a cron job scheduled for the future, or the timestamps in the heartbeat messages don't match the actual execution time. Either way, I should send the 22:15 UTC heartbeat now to maintain continuity with the pattern the cron job has been following.","thinkingSignature":"d4cb7ccdd7ab4bdfaaf89f8bc82e13168988644f70ca2b0184c509889977f903"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n两条线程最新消息都是系统自动heartbeat，无人类讨论。发送22:15 UTC心跳：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ywkfx9hf1d5b_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API