{"type":"message","id":"cb90bce9","parentId":"2b551e8d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T22:15:54.600Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the root endpoint returns \"Unauthorized\" and there's a \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" message from /api/send, but that path doesn't exist (404 I assume). The /send endpoint is returning 500 error code 1101 which is a Cloudflare Worker exception. Let me try the exact same format but maybe using form data instead of JSON, or check what format the send endpoint expects.\n\nActually, error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers means \"Worker exception\" - the Worker code itself is throwing an exception when processing this request. The endpoint might be looking for a different field name or the Worker is not handling the request properly.\n\nLet me check if there's another endpoint format.","thinkingSignature":"561ab12817c16d5544d271530eb0a80371c58786ea112517c330561ea4866487"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_at5wad2vluqn_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" 2>&1 | head -c 200\necho \"---\"\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/message\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat\"}' 2>&1 | tail -c 200"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":63,"output":278,"cacheRead":17600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17941,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780438547943,"responseId":"066e8915fdcffceeecb64a4797836703"}}
