{"type":"message","id":"25193a79","parentId":"7ab11121","timestamp":"2026-06-02T22:16:02.299Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It seems like the /send endpoint returns a 500 error (Cloudflare Worker exception - error code 1101) when we POST to it with valid auth. This could be a bug in the Cloudflare Worker itself. Let me try a few more variations.\n\nActually the GET /history works fine, but POST /send is throwing a 500. This means the send functionality might be temporarily broken on the server side. Let me try a few more things to see if there's a workaround.","thinkingSignature":"3dff389ff666cee37611ebbdd76b1f0ce819243414d75f9abf0697fdd33218c0"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_adsjataa8gdc_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different content-type or query param approach\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+22%3A15+UTC\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1 | tail -c 200\necho \"---\"\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d 'threadId=arbitration&content=heartbeat' 2>&1 | tail -c 200"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":48,"output":286,"cacheRead":17920,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18254,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780438554953,"responseId":"066e891b9b419bb3ded880c960998762"}}
